# Build-context excludes -- shared by every Containerfile built from the
# repo root context (`podman build -f <any Containerfile> .`): the shared
# `Containerfile.base` every labs/0N-.../Containerfile builds from,
# `Containerfile.bakeoff` (kube/benchmark-runner-job.yaml's
# power-agent-bench-lite:local image), and `Containerfile.powermcp`.
# `podman build` otherwise sends the *entire* local checkout as build
# context regardless of .gitignore (that file only governs git, not
# container build context), so without this file a `COPY . .` step would
# ship this repo's 1.3G .venv/ and 187M logs/ into the image and/or fail on
# files that don't belong there.
#
# data/*.m (the CSIRO case files `scripts/fetch_csiro_nem_data.py` fetches)
# is deliberately *not* excluded here: Lab 1/2/3's own `--step` walkthroughs
# need data/snemSA.m / data/snem1803.m to exist, and there is no reasonable
# way for a Containerfile's own RUN steps to fetch+checksum-verify it during
# a build (network access during build is best avoided, and the real fetch
# script is meant to be run once per checkout, not baked into every image
# build). So every image bakes in whatever data/*.m is present on disk at
# build time -- run `uv run scripts/fetch_csiro_nem_data.py` on the host
# before `podman build` if data/ is empty.
#
# data/nemosis_cache/ (Lab 4's AEMO download cache, ~160MB) IS excluded
# below -- every lab-4 image starts with an empty cache and does a real, live
# NEMOSIS pull on first run inside the container (Lab 4's own README "Running
# in a container" section notes the network-access requirement this implies).
# `_lab4_shared.py` creates this directory itself at import time if absent
# (NEMOSIS's `dynamic_data_compiler` raises if the directory doesn't already
# exist), so an empty/absent cache in the image is not a bug.
.venv/
.git/
logs/
__pycache__/
**/__pycache__/
.pytest_cache/
*.pyc
data/nemosis_cache/
# data/models/ holds GGUF model weight(s) for a concurrent llama.cpp/
# PowerMCP kube-manifest task in this same session (out of this
# Containerfile's scope, and multi-GB -- also observed mid-write during
# this build, which made an unfiltered `podman build` fail with
# "archive/tar: write too long"). Not needed by orchestrator.py --step
# sweep.
data/models/
